From 723a238d2222887720ecea8b83b019221ed25120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:47:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Share a rest between two voices of a staff

When two voices of a staff rest together, engravers print one rest in the
middle of the staff; the rhythm algorithm gives it to one voice only. The
other voice's next chord then got the end of that voice's previous chord as
its time, i.e. the time of the rest, a slot to its left, and when the voices
disagreed the lowest time won: the chord, and the chords of the other voice
in its slot, came a beat early and the voices ended short of the measure.

Now MeasureRhythm.voiceEnd: a voice whose last chord (on one staff) ends
exactly where a centered rest of another voice on the same staff starts, in
an earlier slot, would be free at the end of that rest (and of consecutive
shared rests). SlotMapper.endFor uses it, for the times a slot infers, for
checking a mapping and when applying it, only when the narrow slot confirms
that time: its time is known to be that, or another chord of the slot comes
there on its own (from its voice's last chord end, or by beam or tie).
Otherwise the raw end is used, as before (a misaligned or stray rest). In
purgeExtinctVoices a voice resting along with such a rest stays active until
the rest ends, and is over if it does not resume right there. Logged as
"after a rest shared with another voice". Not reconciled with implicit
tuplets (shrinkVoice re-times chords from raw ends; off by default).
